{"sourceSha256": "192eee0e39596cc65a87546ea3cd9e01cebf264fef2e0d199d5b2cc3d7410c11", "text": "Test WRITING SUB-TEST:        MEDICINE\nTIME ALLOWED:                 READING TIME: 5 MINUTES\n                              WRITING TIME: 40 MINUTES\n\n\n\nRead the case notes and complete the writing task which follows\n\n\n\nNotes\nMr Michael Reed is a patient at your GP clinic, Bayview Medical Centre.\n\n\n\nPatient Details\n\nName​:                Mr Michael Reed\n\nD.O.B:                24/10/1979 (39 years old)\n\nAddress:              52 A Wilson Court, Wilson Crescent, Bayview\n\nOccupation​:          Warehouse operative\n                      Picks orders in a large warehouse (includes forklift truck driving,\n                      periods of prolonged standing and sitting, occasional lifting). Works\n                      shifts.\n\n\n\nSocial background: Married - Shamina Reed, 1 child (wife pregnant)\n\nHobbies​:             Rugby, fishing, DIY\n\nMedical history​:     1989 - Appendix removed\n                      1991 - Fracture to wrist (L)\n                      Allergic to penicillin\n\n\n\nCurrent medication\n\n               Diclofenac (non-steroidal and anti-inflammatory drug)\n               Carisoprodol (muscle relaxant, blocks pain)\n\n03/6/19        Hurt back gardening.\n               Took painkillers, went to work, no rest, pain worsening.\n               Presented 2 days post initial strain.\n\f\nX-ray:         No disc problems\n               Diagnosis:     Lower back strain - severe.\n               Treatment:     Exercise: gentle walking daily - ↟ time / distance\n                              Referral to physiotherapist\n                              Prescribed: Diclofenac, carisoprodol\n                              15 days off work - certificate provided for employer\n                              Will review in 2 weeks.\n\n17/06/19       Pt moving stiffly; exercises very painful, but compliant.\n               Walking 10 mins a day.\n               Further 15 days rest prescribed.\n\n\n\n27/06/19       Progressing slowly - ↟ROM - still in pain.\n               Pain after 20 mins sitting / lying down.\n               Very tired after exercise. Pt. worried - not used to being inactive.\n               Further 15 days rest prescribed.\n\n10/07/19       Walking 20 - 25 mins a day.\n               2 more physio sessions left.\n               Pt. still in pain.\n               Prescribed ↟Diclofenac. Pt reluctant - afraid of addiction.\n               Pt. bored, anxious about baby’s arrival.\n               Doesn’t want to lose job. Keen to return to workplace. Employer supportive.\n\n               Fit to work certificate issued: return to work possible with amended duties - no\n               lifting + regular breaks.\n               Letter to OT requesting assessment of w/p (advise on duties can perform\n               etc.)\n\nWriting Task\n\nUsing the information in the case notes, write a letter to Mr Asad Iqbal, an Occupational\nTherapist detailing Mr Reed’s situation and requesting an assessment of his workplace.\nAddress the letter to Mr Asad Iqbal, Golders Park Occupational Health Centre, Bayview.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Test WRITING SUB-TEST:        MEDICINE\nTIME ALLOWED:                 READING TIME: 5 MINUTES\n                              WRITING TIME: 40 MINUTES\n\n\n\nRead the case notes and complete the writing task which follows\n\n\n\nNotes\nMr Michael Reed is a patient at your GP clinic, Bayview Medical Centre.\n\n\n\nPatient Details\n\nName​:                Mr Michael Reed\n\nD.O.B:                24/10/1979 (39 years old)\n\nAddress:              52 A Wilson Court, Wilson Crescent, Bayview\n\nOccupation​:          Warehouse operative\n                      Picks orders in a large warehouse (includes forklift truck driving,\n                      periods of prolonged standing and sitting, occasional lifting). Works\n                      shifts.\n\n\n\nSocial background: Ma